<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biafada</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Beafada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Biafada are a people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea-bissau">Guinea-Bissau</a>, living along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> de Buba and the Corubal. In the 16th and 17th centuries their small kingdoms, such as Guinala, traded with Portuguese and Cape Verdean merchants, but they declined under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>.</p></div>
